      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a script for a period piece set in the Bronx around 1975. We're starting to look at casting for the background/extra roles and I want to make sure the atmosphere feels real. Can you describe what the typical 'street-level' inhabitants of the Bronx were like back then? Like, the kind of people you'd just see hanging out on the corners or walking the sidewalks, to help us get the archetypes right for the crowd scenes.",
